      "vipSummary": {
        "id": 1448640151,
        "html": "<p>SLCO1B1 is one of the key pharmacogenes involved in implementation of pharmacogenomics. The gene encodes the OATP1B1 transporter.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>It is involved in guidelines for statins including CPIC guidelines for <a href=\"/guidelineAnnotation/PA166262221\">atorvastatin</a>, <a href=\"/guidelineAnnotation/PA166105005\">simvastatin</a>, and <a href=\"/guidelineAnnotation/PA166262321\">rosuvastatin</a> (<a href=\"/gene/PA134865839/prescribingInfo\">go to list of all guidelines with SLCO1B1</a>).</li>\n<li>the nomenclature has been set by <a rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://www.pharmvar.org/gene/SLCO1B1\" target=\"_blank\">PharmVar</a></li>\n<li>key variant pages are <a href=\"/variant/PA166154579\">rs4149056</a> also known as c.521T&gt;C (found in SLCO1B1*5 and SLCO1B1*15 and other alleles) and <a href=\"/variant/PA166154547\">rs2306283</a> (also known as c.388A&gt;G and part of *15).</li>\n<li>See the <a href=\"/page/slco1b1RefMaterials\">Gene-specific Information Tables</a> for Allele Definitions (for which variants comprise which star alleles), Allele function assignments (normal function, no function, decreased or increased function etc) and Diplotype-Phenotype Table (for how the alleles combine to form metabolizer phenotypes for PM, NM, UM).</li>\n</ul>\n"
      },
